error[3-0061]: `Slots` is state-only
   ┌─ tuple_struct_errors.fe:91:13
   │
91 │     let _ = Slots(0)
   │             ^^^^^^^^ a state-only type cannot be constructed as a value
   │
   = `Slots` is pinned to storage by its `Pinned` implementation
   = a state-only type lives at its place in storage or transient storage; name it with an access, such as `let m = mut store.balances`, or pass it as a `mut` or view parameter

